//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Package
// $Module name: FTThemeSeed
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-08-13
//
// Description : Seeds ghiFTThemeMode from the saved setting, ONCE, early.
//
//               WHY THIS EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM FTThemeColors.pkg
//               FTThemeColors has to be compiled near the top of the program - the shared files that call its
//               colour accessors are pulled in early - and at that point ghoApplication is not declared yet, so
//               nothing there can read the registry. This package can, because it is Used AFTER
//               cRefactorApplication.pkg. The split is the whole point: accessors early, the registry read later.
//
//               WHY NOT LEAVE IT TO THE HOSTS
//               cFTThemeHost_mixin.pkg seeds lazily, on the first FlexTron host to construct. That covers everything
//               whose colour is applied at RUNTIME, but the FT dialogs colour themselves at CONSTRUCTION - and
//               ProgramSetupFT.dg is Used at DFRefactorFT.src:1352, one line BEFORE the first dialog that owns a
//               host. It therefore built itself with the dark values no matter what the setting said, which is
//               exactly what Nils saw: "the program settings dialog is still dark" (2026-08-13). Seeding here,
//               straight after the application object exists and ~1150 lines before the first dialog, means every
//               construction-time colour already knows the answer.
//
//               The host-side lazy seed stays as a backstop: it is idempotent (both guard on CI_FTThemeUnset) and
//               it still covers any program that Uses a host without Using this.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use FTConstants.h.pkg   // CI_FTTheme*, ghiFTThemeMode, CS_FTThemeSection / CS_FTTheme

Procedure SeedFTTheme Global
    Integer iMode

    If (ghiFTThemeMode <> CI_FTThemeUnset) ;
        Procedure_Return
    If (ghoApplication = 0) ;
        Procedure_Return

    Get ReadInteger of ghoApplication CS_FTThemeSection CS_FTTheme CI_FTThemeDark to iMode
    // A value written by a future version - or a hand-edited registry - must not leave the global on
    // a meaningless number, so anything unrecognised falls back to dark.
    If (iMode < CI_FTThemeDark or iMode > CI_FTThemeSystem) ;
        Move CI_FTThemeDark to iMode
    Move iMode to ghiFTThemeMode
End_Procedure
